<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, meal steady, oil down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, meal steady, oil down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained steady in central Indian markets. Business volume was dull as arrivals and demand were limited. The undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were down by 100 rupees per tonne on limited demand at higher level. Demand from vanaspati units was dull. The undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were steady and quoted at $265-266 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) at west Indian ports for export. Rapeseed extraction was $96-97 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export and was 3,200-3,250 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Rapeseed extraction prices were slightly up on limited supplies. Business volume was dull, and the undertone was steady.</p>
